{"id":39,"date":"2022-11-21T12:28:45","date_gmt":"2022-11-21T12:28:45","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/?post_type=projects&#038;p=39"},"modified":"2025-04-16T00:36:54","modified_gmt":"2025-04-16T00:36:54","slug":"essendon-residence","status":"publish","type":"projects","link":"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/project\/essendon-residence\/","title":{"rendered":"Lorraine Avenue, Essendon Residence"},"content":{"rendered":"\n\n\n    <section class=\"block block-animate project-info\">\n        <div class=\"grid\">\n            <div class=\"grid__details\"\">\n\n                \n                    \n                        <div>\n                            <h5>Client<\/h5>\n                            <p><p>Private Residential<\/p>\n<\/p>\n                        <\/div>\n\n                    \n                        <div>\n                            <h5>Contractor<\/h5>\n                            <p><p>Kennedy Construction<\/p>\n<\/p>\n                        <\/div>\n\n                    \n                        <div>\n                            <h5>Consultant Team<\/h5>\n                            <p><p>Structural &amp; Civil Engineer &#8211; <a href=\"http:\/\/www.adamseng.com.au\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Adams Consulting Engineers<\/a><br \/>\nBuilding Surveyor &#8211; Gibson Dell Building Permits<\/p>\n<\/p>\n                        <\/div>\n\n                    \n                        <div>\n                            <h5>Photographer<\/h5>\n                            <p><p><a href=\"https:\/\/www.yelp.com\/biz\/christopher-alexander-photography-blackburn\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Christopher Alexander Photography<\/a><\/p>\n<\/p>\n                        <\/div>\n\n                    \n                \n                \n                \n                                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n            <\/div>\n            <div class=\"grid__text\">\n                <p>Contextualism comes in many guises. This new residence replaced an existing single-storey weatherboard cottage in a street lined with similar single-storey weatherboard cottages. It stands proudly two-storey, has a flat roof and has a strongly emphasised verticality. At first glance, it is very different from the neighbours. And yet it sits comfortably in its suburban context.<\/p>\n<p>Fundamentally, the owners liked the neighbourhood but not the prevailing house type. They wanted their new house to look just that &#8211; new, and to capture a way of living not possible within the older house types. We achieved this using a considered, relatively radical approach to siting, plan, form, material and colour.<\/p>\n            <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n    <\/section>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    <section class=\"block block-animate two-columns-image\">\n        <div class=\"grid\">\n            <div class=\"grid__image\">\n               <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"619\" height=\"821\" src=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9483-1-16.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"Essendon Residence\u2019s stone outdoor walls with shiny wooden floor\" srcset=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9483-1-16.jpg 619w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9483-1-16-226x300.jpg 226w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 619px) 100vw, 619px\" \/>                           <\/div>\n            <div class=\"grid__image\">\n            <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"620\" height=\"821\" src=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9318-1-16.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9318-1-16.jpg 620w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9318-1-16-227x300.jpg 227w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 620px) 100vw, 620px\" \/>                        <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n    <\/section>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    <section class=\"block block-animate full-width-image\">\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1320\" height=\"879\" src=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9470-1-19.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"Essendon Residence\u2019s lit facade\" srcset=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9470-1-19.jpg 1320w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9470-1-19-300x200.jpg 300w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9470-1-19-1024x682.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9470-1-19-768x511.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1320px) 100vw, 1320px\" \/>    <\/section>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    <section class=\"block block-animate block-quote\">\n        <div class=\"max-sm:w-full ml-auto w-1\/2\">\n            <div>\n                <blockquote>\n\n                <p>The Essendon Residence breaks with the aged norms of its neighbours. It is cranked, boomerang-like in plan so that it maximises precious sunlight.<\/p>\n\n                \n                <\/blockquote>\n            <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n    <\/section>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    <section class=\"block block-animate two-thirds-image\">\n        <div class=\"grid\">\n            <div>\n                <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"853\" height=\"569\" src=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9574-1-19.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"interior details with vinyl floors\" srcset=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9574-1-19.jpg 853w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9574-1-19-300x200.jpg 300w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9574-1-19-768x512.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 853px) 100vw, 853px\" \/>            <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n    <\/section>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    <section class=\"block block-animate two-columns-text-image\">\n        \n        \n        \n        \n        <div class=\"grid mt-[30px] md:mt-[50px]\">\n\n            <div class=\"grid__text space-y-12\">\n                                <div><p>It is split-level, taking advantage of the sloping site. It provides clear and distinct zoning \u2013 separating parents and children, formal and informal living. A gallery-hallway draws occupants into the heart of the home &#8211; an expansive and richly textured kitchen &#8211; from which radiates the stairwell, powder room, laundry, study, cellar, living, dining and north courtyard. The first floor repeats the gallery hallway to link the children&#8217;s bedrooms and rumpus. Internally, the house features warm timbers and bright white giving it a Scandinavian aesthetic that contrasts with the dark, bluestone tile external cladding.<\/p>\n<p>So whilst seeking to set their own mark in the street, the house simultaneously responds to cues from its neighbours, such as adopting a dark coloured roof colour, proportions of the front verandahs and setbacks both front and side.<\/p>\n<p>The Essendon Residence is a distinctive house in the context of its quiet suburban setting. It is a house that is a credit to the owners\u2019 brief and vision.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n                            <\/div>\n            <div class=\"grid__image\">\n                             <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n    <\/section>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    <section class=\"block block-animate two-thirds-image-right\">\n        <div class=\"grid\">\n            <div>\n                <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"853\" height=\"569\" src=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9574-2-3.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"Essendon Residence\u2019s wide view of the dining table to the living room\" srcset=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9574-2-3.jpg 853w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9574-2-3-300x200.jpg 300w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9574-2-3-768x512.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 853px) 100vw, 853px\" \/>            <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n    <\/section>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    <section class=\"block block-animate full-width-image\">\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1320\" height=\"880\" src=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9645-1-19.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9645-1-19.jpg 1320w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9645-1-19-300x200.jpg 300w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9645-1-19-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9645-1-19-768x512.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1320px) 100vw, 1320px\" \/>    <\/section>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    <section class=\"block block-animate project-carousel\">\n\n        <div class=\"swiper swiper-block\">\n\n            \n                <div class=\"swiper-wrapper\">\n                    \n                                        \n                        <div class=\"swiper-slide\">\n                            <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"465\" height=\"641\" src=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9496-37-1.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"Essendon Residence\u2019s lobby lit by the ray of sunshine\" srcset=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9496-37-1.jpg 465w, https:\/\/architect